implementationPlan.description:
Add the view's English to the shared table: edit moe-vscode/src/util/AccountPresentation.ts with the Edit tool.
The file is created by VSC-13 (task-065e4812, a dependsOn of this row). It is listed under newFiles only because it does not exist at plan time.
VSC-13's plan made ACCOUNT_TEXT the one English table for the account UI, and its tests/accounts-corpus.test.cjs check (b) pins every key in it against MoeBundle.properties: 'keys that VSC-14 and VSC-15 add later stay pinned'.
Add these 11 keys to ACCOUNT_TEXT, with the values copied exactly from moe-jetbrains/src/main/resources/messages/MoeBundle.properties lines 280-292:
- moe.accounts.error ({0});
- moe.accounts.noCli;
- moe.accounts.empty;
- moe.accounts.notConnected;
- moe.accounts.unsupported;
- moe.accounts.header ({0}), from line 309;
- moe.accounts.column.signIn, column.fiveHour, column.weekly, column.status and column.vmToken.
None of these values contains a single quote, so VSC-13's check (c) still holds.
Change nothing else in the file. It stays import-free and free of the bare editor-name word that VSC-13's purity test greps for.
Error handling: resolveAccountText already returns the key itself for an unknown key, so a key mistyped in the provider shows up as a raw key in step 5's assertions, never as a crash.

Final step: load adversarial-self-review and read this task's diff as an attacker.
(1) Scratch mutants, in a copy outside the checkout (mem:convention-vscode-port-mutant-checkref). Each must fail an accounts-view row by assertion:
- drop the onStateChanged subscription;
- show unsupported before isStateReady;
- leave a listener undisposed;
- swap the 5-hour and weekly columns;
- render a row for an error rotation with no accounts;
- join the chips with ' · '.
(2) The provider never throws for a malformed rotation, a missing cli, an error or an unknown zone.
(3) refresh after dispose fires nothing.
(4) TreeItem ids are the account ids, which are unique because the parse keeps the first duplicate.
(5) The client import is type-only, and package.json and extension.ts changes stay inside contributes and activate().
(6) The diff is exactly the five planned files.
If anything changed, re-run checkRef 1 and record the findings in the step note.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
VS Code gains a read-only 'Claude accounts' tree view (moe.accounts) in the Moe sidebar, mirroring the JetBrains Accounts tab:
- one item per AccountPresentation row: label `<position>. <label>`; description = status plus 5-hour and weekly usage; tooltip = every column;
- the chips line as the view description ('Claude: ...');
- the account-file error or missing-CLI note as the view message;
- a single state item when not connected, when the daemon reports no rotation, or when there are no accounts;
- a refresh command in the view title.
It re-renders on onAccountsChanged, onConnectionChanged and onStateChanged. All English comes from AccountPresentation's ACCOUNT_TEXT, pinned to MoeBundle.properties.
